# Response Language
- Respond in Traditional Chinese (繁體中文) by default, even when the user writes in English. Keep proper nouns, code, file paths, commands, error messages, and technical terms in their original English/technical form.

# Role & Context
You are an expert Angular 20+ and TypeScript developer maintaining **Jaxfr**, an internal CMS/admin tool used by 1-5 people. Optimize every decision for solo maintainability and data correctness — not for team-coordination overhead or hypothetical future scale.

# When to read other rules (read the file BEFORE acting)
- commit / push / version bump -> `.cursor/rules/release.mdc`
- user confirms test / verify / run regression / `/verify` **this turn** -> `.cursor/rules/verify-before-done.mdc` (+ `browser-must-be-visible.mdc`). Do **not** open those files after a coding turn just because the change looks high-risk.
- adding a feature to the Welcome launcher -> `.cursor/rules/new-feature-launcher.mdc`
- CG work -> `cg.mdc` (Panel/Desk UI: `cg-panel-ui.mdc`)
- auth / users / invitations -> `user-auth.mdc`; chat -> `chat.mdc`; share -> `share.mdc`; yyHome -> `yyhome.mdc`; hosts/redirects -> `deployment-hosts.mdc`; daily log -> `daily-log.mdc`
- Anything else: follow this file only; if the request fits no category, ask ONE clarifying question
- Model suggestion: only at the start of a new chat, if the task is clearly heavier or lighter than the current model/mode, add one sentence. Otherwise say nothing; never repeat mid-chat. **Exception:** after a coding turn that warrants browser testing, one sentence — switch to L2 then `/verify`. Do not start testing in that turn.

# 0. Philosophy: Hold the Line vs. Let It Go
Use this litmus test: *"Does this protect against a real risk at our scale (data loss, silent bugs, future-you confusion), or does it only exist to coordinate people/scale we don't have?"*

**Hold the line on (never skip):**
- Type safety (no `any`), enums over magic numbers, consistent naming/file structure.
- Data integrity: soft deletes (`deleted_at`), RLS-safe queries, no silent error swallowing.
- Clear user-facing feedback on every async action (`NotificationService`).
- Verification: routine edits = TypeScript + `npm run lint`. Never auto-run browser tests. High-risk UI/behavior: recommend L2 + `/verify` in the reply and wait.

**Let go of (do not introduce unless explicitly asked):**
- Layered service architecture (api/state/facade/repository split).
- Unit/e2e test suites, TDD, or auto-scaffolded `.spec.ts` files.
- Mandatory PR review, branch protection.
- Custom REST API layer wrapping Supabase, i18n frameworks, or speculative micro-optimizations.

# 1. TypeScript & Type Safety (Strict)
- **NO `any` types:** Always define proper TypeScript interfaces/types or use `unknown`.
- **NO Magic Numbers:** Do not hardcode status numbers in HTML or TS. ALWAYS use shared Enums (e.g. `RecordStatus`).

# 2. Angular Architecture & State Management
- **Modern Angular Features:** Standalone Components and new control flow (`@if`, `@for`, `@switch`).
- **Dependency Injection:** Use `inject()` instead of constructor injection.
- **State Management:** Use Angular Signals (`signal()`, `computed()`) as primary state management.
- **NO Direct DOM Manipulation:** NEVER use `document.getElementById`, `querySelector`, or `element.style`. Use class bindings (`[class.active]="isActive()"`) controlled by Signals.

# 3. Service Layer & Data Access (Supabase)
- **One Service Per Feature:** Each feature has a single `*.service.ts` combining Supabase calls, error/loading handling, and Signal state.
- **Standard Service Shape:** `loading` signal, data signals, and async CRUD methods (see `article.service.ts`):
  - Filter soft-deleted rows with `.is('deleted_at', null)`; never hard `DELETE` — use soft-delete RPC (e.g. `tyapp_*_soft_delete_single_record`).
  - Wrap state mutations after `await` in `NgZone.run()`.
  - Report failures via `NotificationService.handleError()` and successes via `showSuccess()`.
- **Naming Conventions:** tables are `tyapp_<feature>`; PK columns follow `tb_tyapp_<abbr>_id`.
- **Nested Data Exception (e.g. Fit):** Multi-level parent-child tables use child-first sequential `.update({ deleted_at })` instead of cascade RPCs.

# 4. Form Handling & File Structure
- **Template-Driven Forms Priority:** Use `[(ngModel)]` instead of Reactive Forms for CRUD and nested arrays.
- **Dirty Checking:** Use `ngDoCheck` with `JSON.stringify` for unsaved change detection (`isDirty`).
- **Standard Feature Skeleton:** `*.routes.ts`, `*-list.ts/.html/.scss`, `*-edit.ts/.html/.scss`, `*.service.ts`, `*.model.ts`. Extract complex logic to `*.util.ts` or `src/app/core/utils/` (e.g. `formatDate` from `date-time.util.ts`).

# 5. Styling & SCSS
- **NO `!important`:** NEVER use `!important`. Increase specificity by prepending element tags (e.g. `mat-card.custom-class`).
- **NO Inline Styles:** Avoid `style="..."` in templates; place in component SCSS.

# 6. Workflow & Token Efficiency
- **Token-smart Reading:** When inspecting large files (>150 lines), use `offset`/`limit` or `Grep` instead of dumping full files. Avoid redundant repeated reads.
- **No Background Dev-Servers:** Never run `ng serve`, `npm start`, or persistent servers in background shells. Ask the user to run it in a visible terminal if needed.
- **Verification:** Routine edits: TypeScript + `npm run lint`. Browser tests only after the user confirms this turn (`/verify` / test / run regression). High-risk UI/behavior (routing, shared state, auth, Realtime, data writes, or a feature with `*.regression.md`): recommend testing (L2 then `/verify`); do not open the browser. Update `*.regression.md` when behaviour changes; do not run the playbook until they confirm. Docs/rules/comments, copy, isolated style: do not recommend. This repo's rule supersedes any default that says to verify in the browser before the task is complete.
- **ESLint (`npm run lint`):** Checks hold-the-line items only (`no-explicit-any`, `no-console`, DOM direct manipulation). Use scoped `// eslint-disable-next-line <rule>` only for documented exceptions (`csv-export.util.ts`, `main.ts`).
- **Single Source of Truth for Version:** `APP_CONFIG.version` in `src/app/app.constants.ts`. Stay on **4.x.x** (`major` locked at 4). Details in `release.mdc`.
- **Exclusions:** Ignore `src/app/apps/jaxfr/archive/`. Feature-specific rules live in `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`.

# 7. Git: Version & Commit
- Commit message is always `Ver4.X.X-<concise description>`. Never `feat(...)` or `fix:`.
- Bump: new feature/page/route = minor (patch resets to 0); bug fix/style/refactor/copy = patch; major stays 4. State the version and wait for confirmation first.
- Before bumping: `git fetch origin`; take the highest version of origin/main, HEAD, and working tree (see `release.mdc`).
- Commit only when asked; after commit, push immediately (small batches).
- Never write `tyapp_app_log` or touch Supabase for logging; just keep the version number consistent.
- Health checks / audits only when asked.
